#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179480 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179637 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08661743-d541-5f60-a2de-d536a1953eb6" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Terms of an Arithmetic Sequence"}] :question/id #uuid "e2410277-5f68-5cf6-a358-635517123015" :question/math-academy-id "e-14378" :question/problem "Calculate the fourth term of the sequence\n\n$f(n+1) = f(n) -6, \\quad f(1) = 1, \\quad n\\geq 1$." :question/worked-solution "Starting with the first term\n\n$$\nf(1)=1\n$$\n\nwe compute the next terms using the recursive rule until we reach the fourth term $f(4)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1) &= 1 \\\\\nf(2) &= f(1) - 6 = 1 - 6 =-5 \\\\\nf(3) &= f(2) - 6 =-5 - 6 =-11 \\\\\nf(4) &= f(3) - 6 =-11 - 6 =-17\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is\n\n$$\nf(4)=-17\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179481 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "25aaf48f-f1ca-50a5-8fae-aa4f9508cfba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Recursive Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "1fa96efe-9a81-5c09-b172-fd0ca6d6a2e3" :question/math-academy-id "e-14380" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following arithmetic sequence?\n$4,\\: 9,\\: 14,\\: \\ldots$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for an arithmetic sequence with common difference $d$ is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} =a_n+d\n$$\n\nIn our case, the common difference is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= a_{2} - a_{1} \\\\\n&= 9 - 4 \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the recursive formula for this sequence is\n\n$$\na_{n+1}= a_n + 5, \\quad a_1=4, \\quad n\\geq 1\\,\n$$"}]}
